    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos** serving as our clear offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** boasts the highest efficiency score at 62.61; despite a slight platoon dip against the lefty Weathers, his placement in the two-hole and an incredibly favorable park factor outweigh the handedness mismatch. Crucially, the scouting report indicates a slow delivery from the opposing battery, providing a statistically significant boost to his stolen base potential\u2014a vital metric for us given our aggressive pursuit of speed. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (61.69) is our most efficient play against a struggling arm, as he squares off against Roki Sasaki\u2019s high-xERA 5.30 profile. Even with a projected #5 spot in the order, **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill matchup, making him a prime candidate to over-index on his ATC base projection.\n\nOur peripheral lineup decisions were heavily influenced by the presence of elite arms, most notably the 2.60 xERA of Trevor McDonald. This significantly dampened the scores for **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) and **Andy Pages** (46.31). While **Kyle Tucker** remains a start due to his high floor, the SP skill penalty prevented him from reaching the \"Strong\" tier. **Nolan Schanuel** narrowly avoided the bench, edging out other reserve options because his 47.75 score reflects a neutral platoon environment against Cantillo; he remains a marginal play required by our current depth constraints. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.86) also occupies a \"Marginal\" designation, as his matchup against Rasmussen is neutralized by a difficult SP skill profile and a dynamic platoon disadvantage that suppresses his power ceiling.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the proximity of our depth pieces to the starting threshold, but with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our flexibility is limited. While we have prospects like **Coby Mayo**, **Brady House**, and **Jacob Wilson** waiting in the wings, none surpassed the efficiency markers of our current starters today. We are also monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who are currently inactive due to team off-days. With lineup cards still pending for several games, we are operating with the assumption that **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** will maintain their projected slots; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, we may be forced to cycle through **Jorge Polanco** or **Miguel Vargas** to protect our game caps. We are keeping a close watch on **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Dominic Smith** as potential pinch-hit pivots, though current weather reports suggest no immediate risks to our starters' availability.",
